Native components built into the runtime

Release binaries, the crates.io crates and the npm packages of ACRYL microVMs
embed the following third-party programs and libraries. They keep their own
licences; their source is available at the exact commits below.

  - libkrun (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/libkrun/libkrun
    commit e12b9b3780ffa8df9f3e1797b217d13453479167
  - libkrunfw v5.4.0 (LGPL-2.1-only), https://github.com/libkrun/libkrunfw
    commit e0647fa7a3932c4570fb2c0fd483b9f7a382ebdd, used as the prebuilt
    release files published there. libkrunfw bundles a Linux kernel
    (linux-6.12.87, GPL-2.0-only, source at https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-6.12.87.tar.xz)
    built with the configuration and patches in that commit of libkrunfw.
    Licence texts: LICENSE-LGPL-2.1-only and LICENSE-GPL-2.0-only in that
    repository.
  - e2fsprogs mke2fs (GPL-2.0), https://github.com/tytso/e2fsprogs
    commit da631e117dcf8797bfda0f48bdaa05ac0fbcf7af
  - bubblewrap (LGPL-2.0-or-later), https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap
    commit 9ca3b05ec787acfb4b17bed37db5719fa777834f
  - gvisor-tap-vsock v0.8.7 (Apache-2.0),
    https://github.com/containers/gvisor-tap-vsock

These are separate works that ACRYL microVMs runs or links; the Apache-2.0
licence of ACRYL microVMs does not change their licences.

